From 1bde36877c6dc737c37691b8fa54f25fa6eba16d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:02:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/timer: TCC waveform extension, RAMP2 and dithering (U2213)

The TCC's waveform extension, as a PIC32CM MC00 does it (firmware/hello
APP=tccprobe2..7, checked by tccwave): the output matrix (OTMX), dead
time on the low and high sides (DTIENx, DTLS, DTHS), SWAPx, the pattern
generator with PATTBUF (PATT reads PATTBUF while PATTBUFV), DRVCTRL
INVENx; DSCRITICAL; RAMP2, RAMP2A and RAMP2C with STATUS.IDX;
dithering (CTRLA.RESOLUTION) cycle by cycle. The units an instance
lacks (MchpInstanceInfo.features and .outputs, from the DFP's TCC
parameters) keep their bits at zero. WAVE and PATT synchronize for 4
GCLK_TCC cycles and drop a write made meanwhile, as silicon does.

STOP and the end of a one-shot put each output in its non-recoverable
state (DS 31.6.2.4): NRVx where DRVCTRL.NREx is set, else floating.
STATUS.CMPx keeps its state, but reads 0 eight GCLK_TCC cycles after a
STOP with DIV1. The EV1 pause keeps the outputs.

TC and TCC: each event stored the timer deadline (the tick + 1 ns) as
the new base time, so the counters lost a tick every few hundred events
at 4 MHz. Both keep exact tick instants now (t_base plus a 2^-32 ns
fraction) and round only the deadline up.

mchp_regfile: a SWRST write no longer reports enable-protected bits.

qtest: per-instance units, OTMX, dead time, swap, pattern, WAVE sync,
DSCRITICAL, RAMP2, dithering, STOP state; a long TC run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
